    "title": "Agent account ran SSH",
    "desc": "An agent account executed ssh, scp, sftp, sshpass or an ssh-based git transfer. agent_ssh_access catches the agent reading SSH *files*; this catches the agent *running* SSH. A coding agent talks to its forge over HTTPS through the proxy - it has no host to SSH to, so an ssh exec is lateral movement or exfil. sshpass -p and ssh-copy-id are especially telling (a password handed to ssh, a key being installed on another host).",
